  "story": "Pakistan has electricity demand concentrated at certain times. Instead of simply building more generation capacity, GRIDFLEX identifies consumption that can be shifted, reduced, stored or coordinated. In this run, 10,000 households, 1,000 commercial and 100 industrial users plus 2,000 solar and 500 battery systems form an aggregated flexibility resource. Peak demand falls from 145.5 MW to 140.7 MW (3.3% reduction). Physical power still flows on the grid; the marketplace settles verified flexibility financially."
